## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design end-to-end performance tests spanning multiple subsystems with realistic data flows, backpressure, and failure modes; probes tail latency budgets during promos and how caching, storage, and batch layers interact under stress.

## Key Concepts

- Tail latency
- End-to-end tracing across Redis, Cassandra, embeddings, Spark
- Workload modeling: read/write mix, skew, burstiness
- Backpressure mechanisms: queues, circuit breakers, autoscaling
- Observability: metrics, logs, distributed tracing
- Failure modes: eviction, timeouts, model cold-start

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-load test skeleton (k6)
import http from 'k6/http';
import { check, sleep } from 'k6';
export default function () {
  http.get('https://svc.example/recommend?user_id=' + Math.floor(Math.random()*100000));
  sleep(0.05);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate that cache warmth is not masking data skew?
- What monitoring dashboards and alerting thresholds would you set for p99 across components?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical understanding of GraphQL-specific performance issues, notably nested resolvers and potential N+1 queries, in a beginner-friendly, repeatable way.

## Key Concepts
- GraphQL resolver timings
- N+1 query patterns and detection
- Field-level instrumentation (Apollo tracing)
- Load testing patterns: ramp and spike
- Layer isolation with mocks/replayed traces

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: k6 load test for GraphQL
import http from 'k6/http';
import { check, sleep } from 'k6';
export default function () {
  const payload = JSON.stringify({ query: "{ user(id:1){ id name posts { id title } } }" });
  const res = http.post('https://api.example.com/graphql', payload, { headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' } });
  check(res, { 'status is 200': (r) => r.status === 200 });
  sleep(1);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you detect N+1 without changing application code?
- What instrumentation would you add if you could only modify test data?

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests realism and the ability to validate performance across regions, with realistic traffic mix, TLS/HTTP2 behavior, edge caching, and backpressure.

## Key Concepts

- Global traffic modeling across regions
- TLS handshake cost and HTTP/2 behavior
- Edge caching effectiveness
- Backpressure, queues, and circuit breakers
- Observability with OpenTelemetry, SLI/SLOs
- Soak testing and autoscaling validation

